{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"f440d593-07e0-4e0e-ba86-fead4e4312c3","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have all 7 files read. Let me now proceed to write the L5 horizon summary. This is a massive task requiring careful synthesis across all 6 answers. Let me plan the structure:\n\n1. Problem coverage overview\n2. Classification by experiment environment (GPU/NVIDIA, NPU/Ascend, Accelerator, Simulator)\n3. Classification by method category (Dataflow Design, Compute Unit Organization, Control & Scheduling, Memory Hierarchy, Interconnect/NoC, Hardware Design & Implementation, Simulation & Evaluation)\n4. Detailed Q&A by category\n5. Method relationships\n6. Uncertainties\n\nLet me identify the key methods across all answers and deduplicate them:\n\n**From Q5.1 (Compute Units + Dataflow):**\n- SIMT Core + Tensor Core heterogeneous organization (NVIDIA GPU)\n- Systolic Array + Weight Stationary Dataflow (TPU/NPU-like)\n- 3D Tensor PE Array (GyRot)\n- Reconfigurable Dataflow Architecture (FEATHER NEST + BIRRD)\n- Warp Specialization (Warp-level micro-operator pipeline)\n- Reconfigurable Dataflow (dataflow, layout) co-switching\n- Cross-PE cooperative encoding (MHE-TPE)\n- Concurrent Kernel Execution (CKE)\n- ACS Inter-Kernel Scheduling\n- TMA + mbarrier for async operations\n\n**From Q5.2 (Control + Memory):**\n- GPU Memory Hierarchy (HBM→L2→L1/SMEM→RF)\n- Warp Scheduler (greedy-then-oldest)\n- Thread Block Scheduler (Leftover + Most-Room Policy)\n- TMA (Tensor Memory Accelerator)\n- mbarrier synchronization\n- Hierarchical Software Pipeline (3-level)\n- Double Buffering (inter-tile + intra-tile)\n- Memory Coalescing\n- Warp Specialization (DMA Warp + Compute Warpgroup)\n- DSM (Distributed Shared Memory) on H100\n- FlashFuser DSM Fusion\n- Expert Weight Prefetching (HtoD overlap)\n- MIG (Multi-Instance GPU)\n- μShare non-intrusive colocation\n\n**From Q5.3 (Interconnect/NoC):**\n- 2D Mesh NoC (SambaNova RDN, 3D NMP)\n- Crossbar NoC (Meta MTIA 2i)\n- NVLink + NVSwitch (all-to-all non-blocking)\n- AMD Infinity Fabric (full mesh)\n- Active Interposer + DFBM (chiplet deadlock-free)\n- SoW 2D Mesh (wafer-scale)\n- MCM-GPU Hierarchical Crossbar\n- CoCoTree (binary tree + in-network compute)\n- MixNet (runtime reconfigurable optical-electrical)\n\n**From Q5.4 (Implementation):**\n- Dataflow Architecture (StreamTensor, AMD Versal, SambaNova)\n- GPU Dataflow Execution (Kitsune)\n- Ascend NPU DaVinci Architecture (Tile-based)\n- Focus Architecture (Modular SA add-on)\n- IANUS (NPU-PIM Unified)\n- CuTe DSL (CUTLASS) for GPU kernel development\n- Tandem Processor (GEMM + programmable co-processor)\n- DRX (Multi-Accelerator Chaining)\n\n**From Q5.5 (Simulators/Evaluation):**\n- GPGPU-Sim / Accel-Sim\n- gem5 + DRAMsim3/Ramulator2\n- Mess Simulator\n- Timeloop + Accelergy\n- CACTI 7.0\n- BookSim 2.0\n- McPAT + GPUWattch + AccelWattch\n- Self-developed MoE Multi-Chiplet Simulator (Orders in Chaos)\n- Roofline Model\n- Scale-Sim\n\n**From Q5.6 (Experiment Environments):**\n- GPU platforms: A100, H100, H200, A40, A800, L40S\n- Non-NVIDIA: AMD MI300/MI350, MTIA v2i/v3, Google TPUv4/v5, Ascend 910B\n- Benchmarks: MLPerf, ShareGPT, Azure-Code, VBench, KernelBench, TritonBench\n- Metrics: TTFT, TPOT, TBT, throughput, goodput, SM utilization, MBU, MFU, TDP%, energy per token\n- Profiling tools: NVML, Nsight Systems, NCU, CUDA Events, Triton Proton, MTIA Insight, ROCm Profiler\n\nNow I need to classify by two dimensions:\n\n**Dimension 1: By Experiment Environment**\n- GPU/NVIDIA (includes GPU simulators)\n- NPU/Ascend/TPU\n- Accelerator (custom ASIC, FPGA)\n- Simulator/Modeling Tools\n\n**Dimension 2: By Method Category (L5 hardware architecture)**\n- Dataflow Design & Spatial Architecture\n- Compute Unit Organization (PE Array / Tensor Core / SIMT)\n- Control & Scheduling (Warp Scheduler, Dispatch, Command Processor)\n- Memory Hierarchy & Data Supply (Cache, HBM, SMEM, TMA, 